1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,356
Garrick remembers your work, and knows whose confidences you hold.

2
00:00:04,706 --> 00:00:11,917
An AI chief of staff for your knowledge work, running on the agent you already use. Everything stays in files you own.

3
00:00:13,217 --> 00:00:17,014
Underneath, Claude or Codex does the work, in an app or a terminal.

4
00:00:17,314 --> 00:00:19,746
Every line of work keeps one resume point.

5
00:00:20,246 --> 00:00:21,697
SAM: Open launch plan.

6
00:00:27,502 --> 00:00:31,683
Calls and mail land in your inboxes. It files each one where it belongs.

7
00:00:32,083 --> 00:00:33,576
SAM: Process the inbox.

8
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:43,023
SAM: Both.

9
00:00:46,068 --> 00:00:52,319
Acme and Birch compete, so you've declared a wall between them. You met their carrier, Cobalt, once for each.

10
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:54,042
SAM: Prep me for Cobalt.

11
00:01:00,815 --> 00:01:03,055
The Acme call stays out of Birch's brief.

12
00:01:03,355 --> 00:01:07,728
Walls are rules for the assistant, backed by limited checks before a commit.

13
00:01:08,928 --> 00:01:12,960
SAM: Board said March, and Theo's budget comes Wednesday. Wrap up.

14
00:01:17,215 --> 00:01:22,100
Tomorrow, Claude or Codex picks up from that note, not from a lost conversation.

15
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:28,377
And an optional status page answers two questions: is anything wrong, and where was I?

16
00:01:29,677 --> 00:01:33,410
Your work, remembered, in files you own, with boundaries you declare.

17
00:01:33,910 --> 00:01:34,678
Garrick.
